@prefix cd: <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/> .
@prefix ex: <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level6-statistical-tests> {
  ex:l6-statistical-testing a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Statistical testing"@en, "Statistisches Testen"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-testing-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-testing-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "A statistical test compares a statistic computed from observations with its sampling distribution under a specified null model. A prespecified rejection rule controls an error probability under stated sampling assumptions. The conclusion concerns the target population and experimental unit represented by the design."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-nist-tests ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-hypothesis a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Statistical hypothesis"@en, "Statistische Hypothese"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-hypothesis-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-hypothesis-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "A statistical hypothesis specifies a set of probability models or parameter values for a population. The null hypothesis and alternative are stated before analysing the relevant outcomes. An equality null and a directional composite null define different questions and rejection regions."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-nist-tests ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-alpha a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Significance level"@en, "Signifikanzniveau"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-alpha-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-alpha-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "The significance level bounds the probability of rejecting a true null hypothesis over repetitions of the specified procedure. For a composite null, the bound applies over its parameter space. The chosen level, family of comparisons and direction are properties of the planned procedure."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-nist-tests ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-df a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Degrees of freedom in a test"@en, "Freiheitsgrade eines Tests"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-df-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-df-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Degrees of freedom index the reference distribution associated with independent information remaining after fitting constraints. Centring n independent Normal observations about their estimated mean leaves n minus one residual degrees of freedom. Welch's reference uses a generally noninteger approximation calculated from both variance estimates."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-t ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-p-value a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "p-value"@en, "p-Wert"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-p-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-p-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "A p-value measures how extreme the observed statistic is relative to a specified null reference, using the prespecified extremeness ordering. It is calculated conditional on the null model and assumptions. Estimation and confidence intervals describe effect magnitude and precision alongside this compatibility measure."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-asa ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-t-test a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "t-test"@en, "t-Test"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-t-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-t-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "A t-test standardizes a mean contrast by an estimated standard error. Independent identically distributed Normal errors give exact one-sample and paired t references; the paired test applies to independent pair differences. The pooled two-sample test additionally assumes a common population variance. Welch uses separate variances and an approximate t reference."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-t ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-multiplicity a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Multiple testing"@en, "Multiples Testen"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-multiplicity-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-multiplicity-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "A family of inferential claims requires an error criterion defined for that family. Bonferroni controls the probability of at least one false rejection by allocating the family significance level across tests. Holm's ordered step-down method also controls family-wise error under arbitrary dependence. Prespecified gatekeeping requires a valid procedure for the complete family."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-adjust ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-test a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "F-test"@en, "F-Test"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-f-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "An F-test compares an observed ratio with an F distribution under a null model. For two independent iid Normal samples with equal variances, the ratio of sample variances has numerator and denominator degrees of freedom in the stated order. In Normal linear models with common error variance, nested-model tests compare additional explained variation with the full model's residual mean square."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-var, ex:l6-source-r-anova ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-chi-test a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Chi-square testing"@en, "Chi-Quadrat-Test"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-chi-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-chi-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Chi-square references arise in distinct testing problems. A scaled variance has an exact chi-square reference for iid Normal observations about their estimated mean. Pearson goodness-of-fit and contingency-table tests compare observed with expected counts and ordinarily use asymptotic chi-square references; sparse counts can require exact or model-appropriate Monte Carlo calibration."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-chisq, ex:l6-source-nist-tests ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-mann-whitney a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Mann–Whitney U test"@en, "Mann–Whitney-U-Test"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-mw-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-mw-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "The Mann–Whitney rank-sum test compares two independent samples through their joint ranks or pairwise ordering. The usual exact exchangeability null specifies equal distributions. A common-shape location-shift model supports interpretation as a location or median shift. Ties, discreteness and unequal distribution shapes affect interpretation and calibration."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-wilcox ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-wilcoxon a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Wilcoxon signed-rank test"@en, "Wilcoxon-Vorzeichen-Rang-Test"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-wilcoxon-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-wilcoxon-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "The signed-rank test ranks the absolute nonzero within-pair differences and combines ranks according to their signs. Its conventional location inference assumes independent pair differences with a symmetric distribution. Zero differences and ties need a declared computational convention. A sign test uses signs alone and answers a different question."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-wilcox ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-power a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Statistical power"@en, "Teststärke"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-power-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-power-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Power is the probability that the specified procedure rejects its null at a particular alternative model. It depends on the true effect, variability, number of independent experimental units, direction, significance level and analysis method. Prospective planning evaluates scientifically relevant alternatives and assumptions, with uncertainty in pilot estimates considered."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-power ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-effect a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Effect size"@en, "Effektstärke"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-effect-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-effect-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "An effect size states the magnitude and direction of an estimand in native units or on a declared standardized scale. Mean differences, standardized mean differences and pairwise ordering probabilities describe different targets. The denominator convention, experimental unit and uncertainty belong to the report. Ecological or analytical relevance is assessed against a justified domain-specific criterion."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-asa, ex:l6-source-cliff ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cliff a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Cliff's delta"@en, "Cliffs Delta"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-cliff-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cliff-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "For independently drawn X and Y, Cliff's delta is the probability that X exceeds Y minus the probability that X is smaller than Y. Its empirical estimate averages pairwise signs across the two samples, with ties contributing zero. Positive delta follows the declared X-minus-Y orientation; uncertainty must reflect the dependence among pairs sharing an observation."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-cliff ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-grubbs a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Grubbs' single-outlier test"@en, "Grubbs-Ausreißertest"@de ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l6-grubbs-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-grubbs-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Grubbs' test standardizes the largest deviation from the sample mean under a single-outlier alternative with an otherwise iid approximately Normal background. Its critical value accounts for selection of the most extreme observation. Repeated unadjusted removal changes the error rate. A flag prompts investigation and a documented sensitivity analysis; the sampling record determines the scientific interpretation of the observation."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-nist-grubbs ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-one-t a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "One-sample standardized mean contrast"@en ; cd:latex "t=\\frac{\\bar x-\\mu_0}{s/\\sqrt n},\\qquad \\nu=n-1" ; cd:body "Subtract the hypothesized mean from the sample mean and divide by the estimated standard error; the reference has n minus one degrees of freedom."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-one-t ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-t ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-one-t a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-one-t-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-one-t-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols, units and reference"@en ; cd:body "- **t**: Observed test statistic; dimensionless.\n- **x̄**: Arithmetic sample mean; response unit.\n- **μ₀**: Fixed null-reference population mean; same unit.\n- **s**: Sample SD, using denominator n − 1; same unit.\n- **n**: Number of independent observations; greater than one.\n- **ν (nu)**: Reference degrees of freedom.\n- **√**: Positive square root.\n- **−, /, =**: Subtraction, division and equality.\n\nConditions: independent identically distributed Normal observations, positive variance and fixed reference. Juxtaposition multiplies; subscripts label quantities. Estimated reference uncertainty requires its own model."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-t-p a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Tail probabilities for the selected direction"@en ; cd:latex "p_{>} = 1-F_\\nu(t),\\quad p_{<}=F_\\nu(t),\\quad p_{\\ne}=2[1-F_\\nu(|t|)]" ; cd:body "Read the upper, lower or symmetric two-sided t-reference tail according to the prespecified alternative."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-t-p ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-t ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-t-p a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-t-p-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-t-p-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and tails"@en ; cd:body "p is a dimensionless tail probability. The subscripts >, < and ≠ identify the greater, less and two-sided alternatives for the mean contrast. Fν is the continuous t CDF with ν degrees of freedom, evaluated at the dimensionless observed statistic t; ν follows the selected test. |t| is absolute value. 1 is total probability; 2 doubles the symmetric upper tail. = means equality; − subtraction; brackets group an expression; parentheses enclose function arguments. The formulas use a symmetric t null reference calibrated at the null boundary for a directional composite hypothesis."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-pooled a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Independent means with a justified common variance"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}\\underbrace{s_p^2}_{\\text{weighted variance}}=\\frac{(n_1-1)s_1^2+(n_2-1)s_2^2}{n_1+n_2-2}\\\\t=\\frac{\\bar x_1-\\bar x_2-\\Delta_0}{s_p\\sqrt{1/n_1+1/n_2}}\\\\\\nu=n_1+n_2-2\\end{gathered}" ; cd:body "Pool the sample variances using residual degrees of freedom as weights, then standardize the mean difference."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-pooled ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-t ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-pooled a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-pooled-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-pooled-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and equal-variance model"@en ; cd:body "- **1, 2**: Independent-group indices.\n- **n₁, n₂**: Group sample sizes, each greater than one.\n- **x̄₁, x̄₂**: Group means; response unit.\n- **s₁², s₂²**: Sample variances, denominators n₁ − 1 and n₂ − 1; squared response unit.\n- **sₚ²**: Pooled variance weighted by residual degrees of freedom; p labels pooling.\n- **sₚ**: Positive square root of pooled variance; response unit.\n- **Δ₀**: Null population mean difference, often zero; response unit.\n- **t; ν**: Dimensionless test statistic; residual degrees of freedom.\n- **2; √**: Squaring; positive square root.\n- **+, −, =, fraction bars**: Add, subtract, equal, divide.\n\nConditions: independent Normal samples with one common positive population variance. Juxtaposition multiplies; parentheses group. The underbrace labels the weighted variance."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-paired a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "A paired comparison is a one-sample analysis of differences"@en ; cd:latex "d_i=x_i-y_i,\\quad t=\\frac{\\bar d-\\Delta_0}{s_d/\\sqrt n},\\quad \\nu=n-1" ; cd:body "Form one signed difference per independent pair and standardize its mean against the null difference."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-paired ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-t ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-paired a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-paired-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-paired-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and pairing"@en ; cd:body "- **i**: Original matched batch index.\n- **xᵢ, yᵢ**: Before and end concentration in that same batch; mg/L.\n- **dᵢ; d̄**: Before-minus-end difference; mean of differences; mg/L.\n- **s_d**: Sample SD of differences, denominator n − 1; mg/L.\n- **Δ₀**: Null mean difference, here zero; mg/L.\n- **n**: Independent batches, not individual readings; greater than one.\n- **t; ν**: Dimensionless statistic; reference degrees of freedom.\n- **√; −; =; fraction bars**: Positive square root, subtract, equal, divide.\n\nConditions: independent Normal batch differences with positive variance. Original readings within a batch may be dependent; do not sort them to create new pairs. Subscripts label quantities; parentheses group."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-welch a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Separate sample variances determine Welch's standard error"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}v_j=\\frac{s_j^2}{n_j},\\quad t=\\frac{\\bar x_1-\\bar x_2-\\Delta_0}{\\sqrt{v_1+v_2}}\\\\\\nu=\\frac{(v_1+v_2)^2}{v_1^2/(n_1-1)+v_2^2/(n_2-1)}\\end{gathered}" ; cd:body "Standardize using the sum of the two estimated mean variances and calculate Welch–Satterthwaite degrees of freedom."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-welch ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-t ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-welch a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-welch-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-welch-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and approximation"@en ; cd:body "- **j; 1, 2**: System index; NIR and HPLC-MS.\n- **n_j**: Independent preparations in system j; greater than one.\n- **s_j²**: Sample variance, denominator n_j − 1; squared µg/L.\n- **v_j**: Estimated variance of the system mean; squared µg/L.\n- **x̄₁, x̄₂; Δ₀**: System means; null mean difference; µg/L.\n- **t; ν**: Dimensionless statistic; approximate, possibly fractional degrees of freedom.\n- **2; √**: Squaring; positive square root.\n- **+, −, =, fraction bars**: Add, subtract, equal, divide.\n\nConditions: independent Normal groups, unequal positive variances allowed. Reference is approximate. Juxtaposition multiplies; parentheses group; subscripts identify independent systems."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-bonferroni a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Bonferroni protects a prespecified family"@en ; cd:latex "\\alpha_j=\\frac{\\alpha_{\\mathrm{family}}}{m},\\qquad p_{j,\\mathrm{adj}}=\\min(1,mp_j)" ; cd:body "Divide the family level over m comparisons or compare Bonferroni-adjusted p-values with the family level."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-bonferroni ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-adjust ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-bonferroni a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-bonferroni-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-bonferroni-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and test-family"@en ; cd:body "- **α_family**: Chosen test-family significance level, here 0.05.\n- **m**: Number of planned tests, here three; positive integer.\n- **j**: One test's index.\n- **α_j**: Per-test significance level.\n- **p_j; p_j,adj**: Valid raw p-value; adjusted p-value.\n- **min**: Choose the smaller of the two arguments.\n- **mp_j**: Multiplication of m and the raw p-value.\n- **/, =, parentheses**: Divide, equal, group arguments.\n\nAll levels and probabilities are dimensionless. Test-family membership is prespecified. The union-bound control permits dependent tests; it controls at least one false rejection, not every possible joint decision rule."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-f-ratio a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Two independent Normal-sample variances"@en ; cd:latex "F=\\frac{s_1^2}{s_2^2},\\qquad (\\nu_1,\\nu_2)=(n_1-1,n_2-1)" ; cd:body "Compare the ratio of sample variances with the F reference in the specified numerator and denominator order."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-f-ratio ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-var ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-f-ratio a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-f-ratio-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-f-ratio-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and numerator order"@en ; cd:body "- **F**: Observed variance ratio; dimensionless.\n- **s₁², s₂²**: Sample variances, denominators n₁ − 1 and n₂ − 1; (mg/L)².\n- **1, 2**: Prespecified numerator A and denominator B.\n- **n₁, n₂**: Independent sample sizes, each greater than one.\n- **ν₁, ν₂**: Numerator and denominator degrees of freedom, in that order.\n- **2; −; =; fraction bar**: Square SD, subtract, equal, divide.\n- **Parentheses, comma**: Ordered pair of degrees of freedom.\n\nExact reference: independent Normal samples and equal positive population variances under H₀. The shown alternative is greater A variance, upper tail. A two-sided question needs both tails. Prespecify the ratio orientation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-nested-f a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Additional model terms versus remaining error"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}F=\\frac{(\\mathrm{RSS}_R-\\mathrm{RSS}_F)/(p_F-p_R)}{\\mathrm{RSS}_F/(n-p_F)}\\\\(\\nu_1,\\nu_2)=(p_F-p_R,n-p_F)\\end{gathered}" ; cd:body "Compare the reduction in residual sum of squares per added coefficient with the full model residual mean square."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-nested-f ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-anova ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-nested-f a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-nested-f-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-nested-f-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and nested models"@en ; cd:body "- **F**: Observed dimensionless test statistic.\n- **R, F subscripts**: Reduced and full model.\n- **RSS_R, RSS_F**: Residual sums of squares; squared response unit.\n- **p_R, p_F**: Fitted independent coefficients, including intercept; full has more.\n- **n**: Same observations in both models; exceeds full coefficient count.\n- **ν₁, ν₂**: Numerator and denominator degrees of freedom.\n- **−, =, fraction bars**: Subtract, equal, divide.\n- **Parentheses, comma**: Grouping and ordered degrees of freedom.\n\nExact reference: full-rank nested linear models; independent Normal errors with common positive variance. H₀ sets added coefficients to zero. More flexible fits can explain random scatter; the F comparison calibrates the improvement."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-anova a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "One-way ANOVA tests a joint mean hypothesis"@en ; cd:latex "F=\\frac{\\mathrm{SS}_{\\mathrm{between}}/(k-1)}{\\mathrm{SS}_{\\mathrm{within}}/(N-k)},\\qquad (\\nu_1,\\nu_2)=(k-1,N-k)" ; cd:body "Divide between-group variation per degree of freedom by within-group variation per degree of freedom."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-anova ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-anova ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-anova a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-anova-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-anova-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and global question"@en ; cd:body "SS_between is the sample-size-weighted sum of squared group-mean deviations from the overall mean; SS_within is the sum of squared observation deviations from their own group means. Both use response-unit squared. k > 1 counts groups; N > k counts all independent observations. F is dimensionless; ν₁,ν₂ are numerator/denominator df. Subscripts name sources of variation. − subtracts, fraction bars divide, = states equality and parentheses/comma group ordered df. H₀ sets all population group means equal; exact calibration assumes independent Normal errors with common positive within-group variance. Rejection establishes that at least one population mean differs under the model."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-variance-chi a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "A fixed variance reference gives a chi-square statistic"@en ; cd:latex "Q=\\frac{(n-1)s^2}{\\sigma_0^2},\\qquad \\nu=n-1" ; cd:body "Scale the estimated variance by its residual degrees of freedom and divide by a fixed reference variance."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-variance-chi ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-nist-tests ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-variance-chi a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-variance-chi-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-variance-chi-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and known reference"@en ; cd:body "- **Q**: Observed chi-square statistic; dimensionless.\n- **n**: Number of independent measurements, greater than one.\n- **ν**: Residual degrees of freedom.\n- **s²**: Sample variance, denominator n − 1; (mg/L)².\n- **σ₀²**: Known positive target population variance; (mg/L)².\n- **0; 2**: Null-reference subscript; exponent squares SD.\n- **−, =, fraction bar**: Subtract, equal, divide.\n- **Juxtaposition; parentheses**: Multiply; group n − 1.\n\nExact reference assumes independent identically distributed Normal measurements and a fixed target variance. For an at-or-below null, use equality as the upper-tail boundary. An estimated reference variance instead needs a two-sample model."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-pearson a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Pearson discrepancy for a fixed multinomial model"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}X^2=\\sum_{j=1}^{k}\\frac{(O_j-E_j)^2}{E_j}\\\\E_j=N\\pi_j,\\qquad \\nu=k-1\\end{gathered}" ; cd:body "Add standardized squared observed-minus-expected count discrepancies across k fixed categories."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-pearson ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-chisq ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-pearson a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-pearson-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-pearson-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and count model"@en ; cd:body "- **X²**: Dimensionless Pearson statistic.\n- **j; k**: Category index; number of exhaustive, mutually exclusive categories.\n- **O_j; E_j**: Observed count; positive null expected count.\n- **N**: Total independent particles.\n- **π_j**: Fixed category probability; all probabilities add to one.\n- **ν**: Approximate reference degrees of freedom with fixed probabilities.\n- **Σ**: Sum over categories 1 through k.\n- **2, −, =, fraction bars**: Square, subtract, equal, divide.\n\nCounts, probabilities and statistic are dimensionless. Juxtaposition multiplies; parentheses group. Adequate expected counts support the chi-square approximation. Fitted probabilities require adjusted degrees of freedom and calibration."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-independence a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Pearson statistic and expected cells under independence"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}X^2=\\sum_{i=1}^{r}\\sum_{j=1}^{c}\\frac{(O_{ij}-E_{ij})^2}{E_{ij}}\\\\E_{ij}=\\frac{R_i C_j}{N}\\\\\\nu=(r-1)(c-1)\\end{gathered}" ; cd:body "Obtain expected cells from the margins, then sum squared observed-minus-expected differences divided by the expected count."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-independence ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-chisq ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-independence a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-independence-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-independence-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and sampling units"@en ; cd:body "- **X²**: Dimensionless Pearson discrepancy statistic.\n- **i, j; r, c**: Row/column indices; numbers of categories, each greater than one.\n- **O_ij; E_ij**: Observed cell count; positive expected count under independence.\n- **R_i, C_j**: Row total and column total.\n- **N**: Positive grand total of independent vessels.\n- **ν**: Approximate reference degrees of freedom.\n- **Double Σ**: Sum over every row and column cell.\n- **2; juxtaposition; fraction bars**: Square, multiply, divide.\n- **−, =, parentheses**: Subtract, equal, group.\n\nCounts, degrees of freedom and statistic are dimensionless. Each independent vessel enters one cell. Adequate expected counts support the chi-square approximation; sparse cells need suitable exact or simulation calibration. The vessel is the independent unit."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-u a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Pairwise ordering gives the Mann–Whitney statistic"@en ; cd:latex "U_X=\\sum_{i=1}^{n_X}\\sum_{j=1}^{n_Y}\\left[\\mathbf{1}(x_i>y_j)+\\tfrac12\\mathbf{1}(x_i=y_j)\\right]" ; cd:body "Count how often an X observation exceeds a Y observation, assigning half credit to ties."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-u ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-wilcox ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-u a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-u-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-u-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and U orientation"@en ; cd:body "- **X, Y**: Independent groups on one ordered response scale.\n- **n_X, n_Y**: Positive group sample sizes.\n- **i, j; x_i, y_j**: Observation indices and their measured values.\n- **U_X**: X wins plus half the ties; dimensionless.\n- **Bold 1(event)**: One when the condition holds, otherwise zero.\n- **>, =, +, ½**: Greater than, equal, add, half credit.\n- **Double Σ**: Visit every X–Y comparison.\n- **Brackets; juxtaposition**: Group terms; multiply.\n\nUsual H₀: identical group distributions, exchangeable labels. This example uses an explicitly tie-aware label-permutation reference. Median-shift interpretation additionally needs common distribution shape. Software may report the complementary U."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-signed a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Rank the magnitude and retain the direction of each difference"@en ; cd:latex "d_i=x_i-y_i,\\qquad W^+=\\sum_{i:d_i>0}\\operatorname{rank}(|d_i|)" ; cd:body "Sum the absolute-difference ranks belonging to positive within-pair differences."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-signed ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-wilcox ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-signed a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-signed-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-signed-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols, ties and zeros"@en ; cd:body "- **i**: Original independent pair identity, not sorted-value position.\n- **x_i, y_i; d_i**: Pair readings and their first-minus-second difference; same response unit.\n- **|d_i|**: Absolute difference size.\n- **rank**: Rank nonzero absolute differences; average ranks for ties.\n- **W⁺**: Sum of ranks of positive differences; dimensionless. Superscript + labels this sum.\n- **Σ; colon**: Sum over indices satisfying the condition; such that.\n- **>, −, =**: Strictly positive comparison, subtract, equal.\n- **Parentheses**: Group the rank argument.\n\nUsual shift inference requires independent symmetric differences. Remove zeros before ranking in this convention. Do not independently sort X and Y. Declare tie/zero handling and exact versus approximate calculation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-power a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Power is indexed by a particular alternative"@en ; cd:latex "\\operatorname{Power}(\\theta)=P_\\theta(\\text{reject }H_0)=1-\\beta(\\theta)" ; cd:body "Power at an alternative model parameter is one minus the probability of retaining the null under that alternative."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-power ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-power ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-power a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-power-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-power-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and conditioning"@en ; cd:body "θ denotes a specified true parameter in the alternative model, with the parameter's scientific unit. P_θ is probability over repetitions of the complete design and analysis at θ. H₀ labels the null hypothesis. Power(θ) is its rejection probability; β(θ) its type-II error probability, both dimensionless between zero and one. 1 is total probability; − denotes subtraction; = equality; parentheses enclose events or arguments. The rejection rule, significance level, sample size, variability and sampling model must be fixed to define this function. Evaluate scientifically relevant alternatives prospectively."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-effect a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Cohen's d uses a declared pooled within-group SD"@en ; cd:latex "\\widehat\\Delta=\\bar x-\\bar y,\\qquad d=\\frac{\\bar x-\\bar y}{s_p}" ; cd:body "Divide the oriented independent-group mean difference by the pooled within-group SD."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-effect ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-r-t, ex:l6-source-asa ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-effect a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-effect-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-effect-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and denominator convention"@en ; cd:body "- **Δ̂**: Estimated X-minus-Y mean difference; hat marks estimation.\n- **x̄, ȳ**: Independent-group means; here NIR and HPLC-MS in µg/L.\n- **sₚ**: Pooled within-group sample SD; positive square root of variance weighted by residual degrees of freedom; µg/L.\n- **d**: Uncorrected dimensionless Cohen effect estimate.\n- **p subscript**: Labels pooling.\n- **−, =, fraction bar**: Subtract, equal, divide.\n\nHere pooling defines a descriptive standardisation. The mean test remains Welch. Magnitude guides are conventions; report native units, uncertainty and design. Paired effects use other denominators."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-cliff a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Cliff's delta counts directional wins and losses"@en ; cd:latex "\\widehat\\delta=\\frac{N_>-N_<}{n_X n_Y}=\\frac{2U_X}{n_X n_Y}-1" ; cd:body "Subtract pairwise losses from wins and divide by all cross-group pairs; ties contribute zero."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-cliff ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-cliff ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-cliff a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-cliff-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-cliff-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols, ties and orientation"@en ; cd:body "- **δ̂**: Estimated dimensionless Cliff effect from −1 to 1; hat marks estimation.\n- **N_>, N_<**: Counts of X-over-Y wins and losses.\n- **n_X, n_Y**: Positive independent-group sample sizes.\n- **U_X**: X wins plus half the ties.\n- **>, <**: Strictly greater and smaller comparisons.\n- **2; −; =; fraction bars**: Twice, subtract, equal, divide.\n- **Juxtaposition**: Multiply sample sizes.\n\nTies add zero to the signed balance but stay in the denominator. Positive delta means X tends larger. Pairs sharing observations are dependent; uncertainty follows the original independent units, not the number of comparisons."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l6-formula-grubbs a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Grubbs' two-sided single-outlier statistic"@en ; cd:latex "G=\\frac{\\max_{1\\le i\\le n}|x_i-\\bar x|}{s}" ; cd:body "Divide the largest absolute deviation from the sample mean by the sample standard deviation."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-grubbs ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-nist-grubbs ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-grubbs a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-grubbs-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-grubbs-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and single-outlier model"@en ; cd:body "- **G**: Observed dimensionless maximum standardised deviation.\n- **n; i**: Sample size, at least three; observation index.\n- **x_i; x̄; s**: Observation, sample mean, positive sample SD; all mg/L.\n- **max; 1 ≤ i ≤ n**: Select the largest value over the complete sample.\n- **| |**: Absolute magnitude; checks either extreme.\n- **−, =, fraction bar**: Subtract, equal, divide.\n\nUse all original values to compute mean and SD; sample SD uses denominator n − 1. H₀ is an independent Normal sample; the alternative concerns one extreme. The cutoff accounts for selecting the maximum."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-formula-grubbs-critical a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Selection-aware Grubbs critical value"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}c=t_{1-\\alpha/(2n),n-2}\\\\G_{\\mathrm{crit}}=\\frac{n-1}{\\sqrt n}\\sqrt{\\frac{c^2}{n-2+c^2}}\\end{gathered}" ; cd:body "Obtain an upper t quantile with n minus two degrees of freedom and transform it to the Grubbs critical value."@en ; dct:hasPart ex:l6-legend-grubbs-critical ; cd:hasSource ex:l6-source-nist-grubbs ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-legend-grubbs-critical a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l6-grubbs-critical-symbols ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l6-grubbs-critical-symbols a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and quantile convention"@en ; cd:body "- **n**: Number of observations, at least three.\n- **α**: Prespecified two-sided significance level.\n- **t_(q,ν)**: t quantile at cumulative probability q and degrees of freedom ν.\n- **q; ν**: Here 1 minus alpha divided by twice n; n minus two degrees of freedom.\n- **c**: Abbreviation for that dimensionless quantile.\n- **G_crit**: Dimensionless Grubbs cutoff; crit labels the threshold.\n- **2; √**: Squaring; positive square root.\n- **+, −, =, fraction bars**: Add, subtract, equal, divide.\n\nJuxtaposition multiplies; parentheses group. Reject if G exceeds G_crit under the independent Normal single-outlier model. This is a two-sided cutoff; one-sided procedures use a different allocation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
}

